So, obviously there are tons of different conducts of different 
difficulty, but let's take a mild conduct that is counted by the game: 
veganism.  So, clearly it does cause some inconvenience to be a vegan.  
Poison resist is hard to come byand the lack is occasionally fatal.  The 
other resists should be obtainable before they are an emergency, but 
there are still trade offs.

However, I've probably played at least a hundred vegan chaotic wizards 
and I would be surprised if even eight of them had died in any way 
related to their veganism.  One starved, two were poisoned at a stage 
when they would/should have had resistance and a couple prayed with low 
hit points and were ignored because they'd recently prayed for food.  
Probably at least a couple of those were utterly avoidable too, so do 
people think that  a mild conduct like veganism Does make the game any 
harder?  I mean, it clearly makes it more inconvenient (I would argue 
that the same is true of wishless, by the way) but I don't think that 
most conducts, even those that are kept track of by the game really are a 
measure of skill.  Opinions?

